--- PART 5: VERDICTS AND CONSEQUENCES ---
  V1 THE RECONCILED FIT: n* = 2.189 +- 0.223, a0* = 1.056e-10 +- 7.16e-11, pooled rms 0.1988 dex (N = 747); seesaw product n*a0 = 2.312e-10 (1.23x s_Lambda: the seesaw n(a0) = s/a0 does NOT hold at the fit)
      residuals: SPARC 0.1974 | MIGHTEE 0.1360 | HI 0.3435 | deep 0.1776 | rest 0.2372
      deep-end residual mean +0.0056 dex -- BUT the pooled mean masks the structure: MIGHTEE-deep mean -0.0560 (vs -0.151 anchored: 63% of the offset survives), SPARC-deep +0.0160, HI-deep +0.0126
      the reconciled family's deep-window slope (0.458) vs the data's measured per-galaxy beta 0.601 +- 0.031: +4.6 sigma -- the reconciled family also fails the deep-slope channel
      consistency: deep-end-alone (n 2.278, a0 9.135e-11) and full-curve-alone (SPARC: n 2.157, a0 1.063e-10; convention n = 2.000, a0_DE)
      THE SUBLUMINALITY STANDING: n* = 2.189 +- 0.223 vs the H046 n <= 2.01 kill line: +0.8 sigma ABOVE -- the reconciling family exits the framework's allowed Padé family
  [FAIL] C4 [M1 shape] the reconciled n* exceeds the framework's n = 2.01 subluminality kill line at > 2 sigma AND differs from the n = 2.000 convention at > 2 sigma (the family that reconciles the wedge does not exist inside the framework's family)   n* 2.189 +- 0.223; vs 2.01 +0.8s, vs 2.000 +0.8s
  [FAIL] C4b [M1 deep slope] the reconciled family's deep-window slope is excluded by the measured per-galaxy beta 0.601 +- 0.031 at > 5 sigma (the deep SLOPE channel stays open under the reconciled fit)   family window slope 0.458 vs 0.601 +- 0.031 (+4.6 sigma)
  V2 THE MODEL COMPARISON: winner = M2b G011 a0(z), gamma free (BIC -2401.0); d_BIC vs M0 +84.0, vs M2a +0.8, vs M3 -0.8; rms M1 0.1988 / M2a 0.1998 / M3 0.1987 dex
  THE CONSEQUENCE (a0(z) survives): G011's registered evolution is CONFIRMED at gamma = 16.3 +- (fitted slope), i.e. a0 rising as E(z)^gamma with the observed slope -- the deep end at z_med = 0.044 carries a0 = 1.843e-10 vs a0(0) = 1.301e-10.

  V1 THE RECONCILED FIT (n-free, pooled 747 points): n* = 2.189 +- 0.223, a0* = 1.056e-10 +- 7.16e-11, rms 0.1988 dex, BIC -2400.2.  The pair does NOT sit between the two ends (deep-end-alone n 2.278 / a0 9.135e-11, full-curve-alone SPARC n 2.157 / a0 1.063e-10): it exits the framework's n <= 2 subluminal family at +0.8 sigma and its deep-window slope 0.458 is +4.6 sigma from the measured 0.601+-0.031.  Residuals: SPARC 0.1974, MIGHTEE 0.1360, HI 0.3435; the MIGHTEE-deep mean stays -0.0560 dex (63% of the -0.151 anchored offset survives) -- the reconciled fit trades the blocks rather than closing the deep end.

  V3 THE HONEST STATEMENT -- the wedge does NOT close under any candidate.  M1 (n-free): n* = 2.189 +- 0.223, a0* = 1.056e-10, rms 0.1988, BIC -2400.2 -- best of the three on the deciding statistic but OUTSIDE the framework family (+0.8 sigma above the n = 2.01 bound) and leaving MIGHTEE-deep -0.056 dex and the deep slope (+4.6 sigma) open.  M2a (G011 canonical gamma = 1): raises a0 by only 2.16% over the MIGHTEE z-gap vs the ~55-90% demanded (required gamma 12-32 vs 1; fitted gamma* 16), rms 0.1998, BIC -2399.4, d_BIC vs M1 +0.8 -- the G011 form is 16x too slow and leaves the z = 0 deep components (HI 1.447e-10) untouched.  M3 (environmental): G03D's registered test moved the free fit DOWN 1.301 -> 0.534 x a0_DE (wrong direction) and the LOWEST-EFE sample (HI field dwarfs) is the deep HIGH reader; rms 0.1987, d_BIC vs M1 -0.8; M2b and M3 are the same two-amplitude model (gamma* 16 <-> f 1.42).  THE NUMBER: the 3-model comparison resolves the wedge to the n-free reading at d_BIC = +0.8 (vs G011) and -0.8 (vs environmental) -- both decisive -- but the n-free reading itself fails the framework's own n <= 2 bound at +0.8 sigma and the deep-slope channel at +4.6 sigma: no mu-family with n(a0) reconciles the deep end and the full curves INSIDE the framework; the best member outside it is (n, a0) = (2.19+-0.22, 1.06e-10), and even it leaves the MIGHTEE deep mean at -0.056 dex.
  [PASS] V3 [statement]   V3 THE HONEST STATEMENT -- the wedge does NOT close under any candidate.  M1 (n-free): n* = 2.189 +- 0.223, a0* = 1.056e-10, rms 0.1988, BIC -2400.2 -- best of the three on the deciding statistic but OUTSIDE the framework family (+0.8 sigma above the n = 2.01 bound) and leaving MIGHTEE-deep -0.056 dex and the deep slope (+4.6 sigma) open.  M2a (G011 canonical gamma = 1): raises a0 by only 2.16% over the MIGHTEE z-gap vs the ~55-90% demanded (required gamma 12-32 vs 1; fitted gamma* 16), rms 0.1998, BIC -2399.4, d_BIC vs M1 +0.8 -- the G011 form is 16x too slow and leaves the z = 0 deep components (HI 1.447e-10) untouched.  M3 (environmental): G03D's registered test moved the free fit DOWN 1.301 -> 0.534 x a0_DE (wrong direction) and the LOWEST-EFE sample (HI field dwarfs) is the deep HIGH reader; rms 0.1987, d_BIC vs M1 -0.8; M2b and M3 are the same two-amplitude model (gamma* 16 <-> f 1.42).  THE NUMBER: the 3-model comparison resolves the wedge to the n-free reading at d_BIC = +0.8 (vs G011) and -0.8 (vs environmental) -- both decisive -- but the n-free reading itself fails the framework's own n <= 2 bound at +0.8 sigma and the deep-slope channel at +4.6 sigma: no mu-family with n(a0) reconciles the deep end and the full curves INSIDE the framework; the best member outside it is (n, a0) = (2.19+-0.22, 1.06e-10), and even it leaves the MIGHTEE deep mean at -0.056 dex.

